@liggitt I can think of two alternative things to test:
1. Test that [checkPreconditions(...)](https://github.com/matte21/kubernetes/blob/clarify-error-message/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/storage/etcd3/store.go#L382), the new unexported function that this PR adds and that produces the error messages, returns the correct error message.
2. Test that the store's GuaranteedUpdate (AKA the function that actually performs the update and that invokes [checkPreconditions(...)](https://github.com/matte21/kubernetes/blob/clarify-error-message/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/storage/etcd3/store.go#L382)) returns the correct error message.

Option 1 results in simpler tests that probably execute faster and are closer to the code that produces the errors;
the problem with it is that if [checkPreconditions(...)](https://github.com/matte21/kubernetes/blob/clarify-error-message/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/storage/etcd3/store.go#L382) gets removed due to future refactorings and the error messages go back to the old, confusing version, the test does not catch the regression. That is why I favor option 2. What do you think?
